<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <OutputPath>bin\$(Configuration)\</OutputPath>
    <MSBuildWarningsAsMessages>NETSDK1069</MSBuildWarningsAsMessages>

    <PackageId>$(AssemblyName)</PackageId>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Symprex/blueprint</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>See https://github.com/Symprex/blueprint/releases for more info</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageBaseTags>API;CQRS;Blueprint;Rest</PackageBaseTags>
    <PackageTags>$(PackageBaseTags);SourceGenerator;OpenAPI;HATEOAS;AspNetCore</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>

    <!-- Restated rather than inherited, for the same reason as WarningsNotAsErrors below: the
         repository-root Directory.Build.props never applies under src/. Without these, NuGet fills
         <authors> with the package ID. Each packable project sets its own <Description>. -->
    <Authors>Symprex</Authors>
    <Company>Symprex Limited</Company>
    <Product>Blueprint</Product>
    <Copyright>Copyright © Symprex Limited</Copyright>

    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>

    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors Condition="'$(IsTestProject)' != 'true' and '$(TreatWarningsAsErrors)' == ''">true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>

    <CodeAnalysisRuleset>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Rules.ruleset</CodeAnalysisRuleset>
    <CodeAnalysisDictionary>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)CustomDictionary.xml</CodeAnalysisDictionary>

    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);JETBRAINS_ANNOTATIONS</DefineConstants>

    <!-- Restated rather than inherited: this is the nearest Directory.Build.props to every
         project under src/, so MSBuild never walks up to import the repository-root file, and
         the root's own <WarningsNotAsErrors> for NU190x silently never applied here (a defect,
         not a policy choice — the root file's comment already states the intended policy). A
         full <Import> of the root file was considered instead but rejected: several projects
         here (e.g. Blueprint.Runtime, Blueprint.SourceGenerator) already carry their own direct
         `JetBrains.Annotations` PackageReference, and the root file adds the same reference
         again, which raises NU1504 (duplicate PackageReference) under TreatWarningsAsErrors.
         Restating just this one property is the minimal fix.

         Advisories are still discovered and still reported — this only keeps them warnings
         instead of build errors, matching the root's documented intent: manage vulnerabilities
         outside the build system rather than let a newly-published advisory break an unrelated
         build the next morning. This is not a blanket "ignore audits" switch; Blueprint.Codemod's
         own NU1903 was fixed with a direct version pin, not this list.

         The Marten case in particular is closed, not open: GHSA-vmw2-qwm8-x84c's first patched
         version is 8.37.0, with no 6.x backport, and D1 (approved) pins Marten down to 6.4.2
         deliberately for Signature365 parity. Signature365's own epic (Symprex/Signature365#6601)
         analysed this exact advisory and found it unreachable there — Marten's full-text-search
         methods are never called, and the one full-text index configured passes no `regConfig` —
         so the SCA alert stays open for the duration of the 6.4.2 pin on that basis, not because
         auditing was weakened here. Do not read this as an invitation to move Marten to 8.x. -->
    <WarningsNotAsErrors>NU1901;NU1902;NU1903;NU1904</WarningsNotAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="StyleCop.Analyzers" Version="1.2.0-beta.556" PrivateAssets="All" IncludeAssets="runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers"/>

    <AdditionalFiles Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Stylecop.json">
      <Link>Stylecop.json</Link>
    </AdditionalFiles>

    <AdditionalFiles Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Rules.ruleset">
      <Link>Rules.ruleset</Link>
    </AdditionalFiles>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Every package carries the same short readme (nuget.org renders it on the package page, and
       its links are absolute because relative ones break there). It also carries the LICENSE and
       NOTICE: Apache 2.0 section 4 requires a redistributed copy to include both, and the
       PackageLicenseExpression above names the licence without shipping its text. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' == 'true'">
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)PACKAGE-README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="README.md" Visible="false" />
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Visible="false" />
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\NOTICE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Only required during CI builds — a deterministic build path baked into the PDB is only
       useful (and only reproducible) from a clean CI checkout. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">
    <DebugSymbols>true</DebugSymbols>
    <DebugType>portable</DebugType>

    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild>true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- MinVer and SourceLink used to be gated behind GITHUB_ACTIONS as well, which meant a local
       `dotnet pack` produced an unversioned package with no RepositoryUrl at all — and it is
       RepositoryUrl (populated by PublishRepositoryUrl + SourceLink below) that GitHub Packages
       uses to route a pushed package to this repository. Both now apply everywhere so a local
       pack matches what CI produces.

       There are no git tags in this repository yet. MinVer's default floor with no tag is
       0.0.0, and three of these package IDs (Blueprint.Testing, Blueprint.Http,
       Blueprint.Tasks.Hangfire) already exist on nuget.org at 0.8.4 from the upstream fork
       (barclayadam/blueprint) — a 0.0.0-alpha.* here would be a confusing, lower-than-upstream
       floor even though Signature365 never resolves those from nuget.org (packageSourceMapping
       keeps it pinned to GitHub Packages; see D6). MinVerMinimumMajorMinor sets a 0.1 floor
       instead, so an untagged build here versions as 0.1.0-alpha.0.<height>+<sha>. The first
       real release is cut by pushing tag v0.1.0, deliberately, once this package has been
       verified end-to-end — not part of this change. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <MinVerTagPrefix>v</MinVerTagPrefix>
    <MinVerMinimumMajorMinor>0.1</MinVerMinimumMajorMinor>
    <MinVerDefaultPreReleaseIdentifiers>alpha.0</MinVerDefaultPreReleaseIdentifiers>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MinVer" Version="5.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" IncludeAssets="runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive"/>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="1.1.0-beta-20204-02" PrivateAssets="All" IncludeAssets="runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers"/>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
